==Battleground==
*2 [[Henry|Henries]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Tackey]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~14.67 seconds<sup>400f~440f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Henry will stop most of your units, so bring fast attackers such as [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]. Try to get the H. Nahs to stack in front of the enemies and sync up, then call in [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to attack them all at once. Henry has low attack power but a long [[Freeze]], so you can easily hit the Cat Deploy Limit, making timing more difficult. The H. Nahs are there to help with that, but not by much. Fast meatshields matter more here in order to slip through and get to the Henrys, so bring along [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] as they are faster than your average meatshield, meaning that they can slip through much easier.

Alternatively, you can cheese the stage using Courier Cat, Manic Lion Cat, and Awakened Bahamut Cat.

Another cheese is using [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] (near or at level 40 is recommended for 2/3 crowns), Awakened Bahamut Cat, and Manic Lion Cat ([[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazy Hearts]] is optional). Wait for the first Mooth to spawn, send one Butterfly Cat when it is at least a quarter way to your base. Then wait for Butterfly Cat to kill the second Mooth and send out Awakened Bahamut Cat, then spam Manic Lion Cat until the base is down.

==Trivia==
*Weeping Dunes' name is derived from ''naki suna'' (泣き砂, "weeping sand"), one of the Japanese terms for [[wikipedia:Singing sand|singing sand]] and the "Song of Dunes", a natural phenomenon wherein sand dunes emit a loud, persistent sound when disturbed under the right conditions.

